  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Pride Of Cucamonga (x3)** (1 review, 1 other source): Notes Phil didn't play it live until after Garcia had died; Acoustic version with Phil alone on guitar breaking the song down; same master source as the Gans DHH version, but not that copy [2][5]\n- **US Blues** (2 reviews): Says it ended up in the encore slot because it didn't bridge well into other songs; Disputes the idea that it was relegated to encores, calling it a big radio hit [3][4]\n- **Unbroken Chain** (1 review): Says the band brought it out fairly late in their career [3]\n- **Money Money** (1 review): Calls it Weir's answer to Loose Lucy; on live versions Donna sings it forcefully [5]\n- **Scarlet Begonias** (1 review): Calls it the most danceable tune [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Pride Of Cucamonga (x3)**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [6]\n- **Money Money**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [6]\n- **Scarlet Begonias + Pride of Cucamonga**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Money Money**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [6]\n- **Loose Lucy + US Blues**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Unbroken Chain, Unbroken Chain, Unbroken Chain, Crazy Fingers [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1974-03-01.152494.mars-hotel-outttakes-unsurpassedvolume8.flacf** (recommended): source not stated; 10 songs; 66 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Spectral view indicates a 32k DAT source; a brief burst of digital static at track 1, 1:24 was reduced to 10% [1]\n- **gd1974-03-01.152493.Mars-Hotel-Outtakes-gadsden-cousinit-onemoreshot.shnf**: source not stated; 8 songs; 38 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1974-03-01.152494.mars-hotel-outttakes-unsurpassedvolume8.flacf**: source: Unsurpassed Volume 8; Label: Dead Man CatalogNo: DM027 > eac > wav > flac [1]. Also: Believed to be the source of disc 1 of another circulating copy, which had its digital static silenced and its sound compressed and harsher [1]\n- **gd1974-03-01.152493.Mars-Hotel-Outtakes-gadsden-cousinit-onemoreshot.shnf**: source: MSR>?>Bill Gadsden Reel>C>DAT>WAV>SHN [2]. Also: Source came from Bill Gadsden, who no longer had his copy and could give no earlier lineage [2]",
